# Cursor Rules for RealtimeVoiceChat Docker Compose Development

## Development Environment Setup
- Always run the application using Docker Compose with development configuration
- Use `docker-compose-dev.yml` for development environment
- Use `.env` file for environment variables (especially PORT)
- Mount current directory to Docker container for live code changes
- No need to rebuild Docker when code changes

## Docker Compose Configuration
- Use `docker-compose -f docker-compose-dev.yml up` to start the application
- Use `docker-compose -f docker-compose-dev.yml down` to stop the application
- Use `docker-compose -f docker-compose-dev.yml logs -f` to view logs
- Use `docker-compose -f docker-compose-dev.yml restart` to restart services

## Environment Variables
- Load PORT from `.env` file
- Mount current directory to `/app` in container
- Enable hot reloading for development

## File Structure
- `.env` - Environment variables (PORT, etc.)
- `docker-compose-dev.yml` - Development Docker Compose configuration
- `docker-compose.yml` - Production Docker Compose configuration
- `Dockerfile` - Container definition
- Volume mount: `.:/app` for live code changes

## Development Workflow
1. Make code changes in the current directory
2. Changes are automatically reflected in the running container
3. No need to rebuild Docker image for code changes
4. Use `docker-compose -f docker-compose-dev.yml restart` only for environment variable changes

## Commands to Remember
```bash
# Start the application (development)
docker-compose -f docker-compose-dev.yml up -d

# View logs (development)
docker-compose -f docker-compose-dev.yml logs -f

# Stop the application (development)
docker-compose -f docker-compose-dev.yml down

# Restart services (development)
docker-compose -f docker-compose-dev.yml restart

# Rebuild and start (only needed for Dockerfile changes)
docker-compose -f docker-compose-dev.yml up --build
```

## Documentation Management
- Always update `./docs/INSTALL.md` with the latest installation steps
- Keep installation instructions synchronized with current Docker Compose setup
- Document any new environment variables or configuration changes
- Include troubleshooting steps for common issues
- **ALWAYS update `./docs/TROUBLESHOOT.md` after resolving any errors or issues**
- Document error symptoms, root cause, and resolution steps in troubleshooting guide
- Keep troubleshooting documentation synchronized with current codebase and Docker setup

## Best Practices
- Always check `.env` file exists and has required variables
- Use volume mounts for development, not for production
- Keep Docker Compose configuration in version control
- Use `.dockerignore` to exclude unnecessary files from build context
- Maintain up-to-date documentation in `./docs/INSTALL.md`
- **Create and maintain comprehensive troubleshooting guide in `./docs/TROUBLESHOOT.md`**
- Use `docker-compose-dev.yml` for development and `docker-compose.yml` for production 